# One answer to "what is a line ending in this repository".
#
# Without this file the answer was "whatever the last tool to touch it did",
# and the repository held 76 all-CRLF files, 49 all-LF files, and 6 with both.
# That is invisible until you edit one: a two-line change to a mixed file came
# back as a 318-line diff, twice, because the editor settled the whole file on
# the way past. Every line of that noise is a line nobody reviews.
#
# So: every text file is stored with LF, and checked out with whatever this
# machine wants. Windows checkouts still get CRLF on disk under
# core.autocrlf=true; nothing about how you edit has to change.
*               text=auto

# Batch files are the exception worth naming. Windows runs them line by line
# off disk, and a stray LF-only continuation has been known to break a label
# jump, so these are pinned to CRLF in the working tree regardless.
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf
